2026-11-10T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2488) 'Can a garment become independent bodies that swing on their own?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2488  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2488) 'The product avatar wears clothes.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2488  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2488) 'Hair, skirts, belts and scarves are separate parts with cavities and non-manifold edges.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2488  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2488) 'A plain surface net cannot see across disconnected components.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2488  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2488) 'Garments must move independently.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2488  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2488) 'Skin weights attach; they do not swing the cloth.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2488  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2488) 'Read DETAILS for the part-to-body mapping and the first gate.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2488  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-10T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2488) 'Cage-wrapped segmentation net and independent garment bodies for VRM spring-bone rigs
